{"id": "internet-choice-lobbyists-parks-payment", "title": "A lobbyist’s firm paid for schoolyards the day it sought support for a bill", "seconds": 57.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "made": "2026-11-27", "key": "db8aa812a3ec26a6", "words": 164, "beats": [{"scene": "c", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["status"], "text": "It's a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 1.57, "shot": "lead", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["Who", "paid", "for", "schoolyards?"], "sub": "An investigative lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.33, 0.65, 0.83, 0.91]}, {"scene": "c", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "On October eighteenth, an AT&T lobbyist discussed fiber with Supervisor Mark Farrell.", "t0": 1.69, "t1": 6.57, "shot": "s0", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "oct", "kicker": "October 2016", "text": "Fiber optic network", "mark": "monitor"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.65, 1.21, 1.45, 1.82, 1.94, 2.16, 2.63, 3.08, 3.45, 3.6, 4.23, 4.49]}, {"scene": "c", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Farrell introduced a bill giving tenants more choice of internet providers that day.", "t0": 6.69, "t1": 10.67, "shot": "s1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "file", "kicker": "File 161110", "text": "Providers and tenants", "mark": "October 18"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.87, 0.96, 1.24, 1.52, 1.89, 2.11, 2.45, 2.55, 2.91, 3.44, 3.63]}, {"scene": "c", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "In November, the same lobbyist sought support for an amendment.", "t0": 10.79, "t1": 13.83, "shot": "s2", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "nov", "kicker": "November 14", "text": "Internet service provider choice amendment", "mark": "support"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.8, 0.98, 1.27, 1.71, 1.98, 2.38, 2.53, 2.63]}, {"scene": "c", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "That day his firm, Lighthouse Public Affairs, paid $5,000 to Parks Alliance.", "t0": 13.95, "t1": 18.61, "shot": "s3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$5,000", "label": "Lighthouse Public Affairs to Parks Alliance"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.44, 0.61, 0.94, 1.38, 1.7, 2.5, 2.81, 3.1, 3.47, 3.78, 3.9, 4.18]}, {"scene": "c", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "Farrell disclosed asking for the money for a Shared Schoolyards fundraiser.", "t0": 18.73, "t1": 22.21, "shot": "s4", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "payment", "kicker": "Form 803", "text": "Shared Schoolyards fundraiser", "mark": "page 2"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.34, 0.88, 1.17, 1.3, 1.43, 1.72, 1.89, 1.97, 2.29, 2.87]}, {"scene": "v", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "Farrell voted yes on December 13. All ten seated supervisors approved the ordinance.", "t0": 22.43, "t1": 27.54, "shot": "s5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "10–0", "label": "Final vote, District 8 vacant"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.68, 0.96, 1.07, 1.48, 2.61, 2.9, 3.15, 3.47, 4.19, 4.56, 4.68]}, {"scene": "v", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "Some tenants had just one provider. The ordinance gave qualifying providers access.", "t0": 27.66, "t1": 32.09, "shot": "s6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "vote", "kicker": "Ordinance 250-16", "text": "Access for eligible providers", "mark": "findings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.62, 0.8, 1.05, 1.23, 2.05, 2.23, 2.64, 2.87, 3.39, 3.93]}, {"scene": "v", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "The vote awarded no city contract to AT&T.", "t0": 32.21, "t1": 35.17, "shot": "s7", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "vote", "kicker": "Ordinance 250-16", "text": "Access for eligible providers", "mark": "findings"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.46, 0.9, 1.09, 1.4, 1.92, 2.06, 2.48, 2.6]}, {"scene": "r", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "Ethics staff later examined $882,500 of fundraising.", "t0": 35.39, "t1": 40.31, "shot": "s8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$882,500", "label": "Farrell’s fundraising for Parks Alliance reviewed by staff"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.75, 1.07, 1.58, 1.82, 2.17, 2.77, 3.23, 3.55, 3.83, 4.2, 4.3]}, {"scene": "r", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "Staff said the rules then allowed this request. They found no exchange for a vote.", "t0": 40.43, "t1": 44.54, "shot": "s9", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "report", "kicker": "Ethics staff review", "text": "Fundraising from restricted sources", "mark": "pages 11–12"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.35, 0.54, 0.65, 0.93, 1.1, 1.4, 1.58, 2.49, 2.72, 2.99, 3.16, 3.63, 3.79, 3.87]}, {"scene": "r", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[3]"], "text": "Most of the fundraising would still qualify under the rule staff proposed.", "t0": 44.66, "t1": 48.05, "shot": "s10", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "report", "kicker": "Staff assessment", "text": "Most fundraising would remain allowed", "mark": "page 12"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.35, 0.46, 1.03, 1.19, 1.46, 2.01, 2.21, 2.33, 2.57, 2.86]}, {"scene": "r", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "On January 23, 2022, the city barred requests to specified interested parties.", "t0": 48.17, "t1": 53.86, "shot": "s11", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "reform", "kicker": "File 201132", "text": "Restrictions on requests", "mark": "January 23, 2022"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.71, 1.53, 1.86, 2.81, 2.97, 3.29, 3.61, 4.09, 4.22, 4.86, 5.25]}, {"scene": "r", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 53.98, "t1": 56.33, "shot": "end", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.38, 0.5, 0.58, 1.3, 1.53, 1.63]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"c": "Two reported contacts", "v": "A tenant-choice vote", "r": "The rule in force"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "contrast"}